The README's inline script (round 25), run unchanged except that for each sampled key row n with
attention mass sum_m pE < 1/8 it also prints: mean over j of dVTol; the eta16 part of the floor
(#allowed pairs * 2^-25 * mean|dO|); the whole accumulation term accB(T, sum_m p16L*lm dO) (mean
over j); the number of allowed pairs whose p16L is lifted to exactly 2^-14; and T. Benchmark
inputs only (N_CTX = 2^14, std 1, sm_scale 1.3, default_rng(20)). The lift's own excess on a row is
about nLifted * 2^-14 * ((1+rho)^T - 1) * mean|dO| (e.g. row 8197: 70 * 6.1e-5 * 4.3e-3 * 0.8 =
1.5e-5, against an eta16 floor of 3.9e-4).

